<#
CNA_Create_Identity_WebApp_From_Json_RegularUser_Final_v2.ps1

Best-preferred flow:
1) Login to PAS as a regular user
2) Validate the PAS account in the target Safe using exact match only
3) Login to Identity as the same regular user
4) Import the app from template
5) Poll GetApplication until the app is visible/ready
6) Build update payload from the actual returned app object
7) Call UpdateApplicationDE
8) Apply direct application permissions to the target group

Changes requested:
- Template default changed to GCP-AccountsTemplate
- Identity password challenge reuses the same password entered initially
- Update path now uses GetApplication after create, which aligns better with CyberArk's documented update flow
#>

[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    # ===== PAS / Privilege Cloud auth path =====
    [string]$IdentityTenantURL    = 'https://aat4012.id.cyberark.cloud',

    # ===== Identity app-management API path =====
